        <mxCell id="app-team-note" value="Owned/managed by: Application / IDP Team&#xa;Only action needed: pass the Network account&#39;s execute-api&#xa;VPCE ID as the ApiGatewayVpcEndpointId stack parameter." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#545B64;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="490" width="290" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-box" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#545B64;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="220" y="600" width="1100" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-title" value="Path A — resolution &amp; onboarding flow (no custom domain)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="235" y="608" width="600" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-text" value="1. The execute-api Interface VPCE already exists in the Network account with PrivateDnsEnabled=true — this is the SAME endpoint already used today by the raw execute-api URL.&#xa;2. No new Network-account resource is created for onboarding a new app/environment. The Network team supplies ONE value: the existing VPCE ID.&#xa;3. In the Application account, the App/IDP team passes that VPCE ID as the ApiGatewayVpcEndpointId CloudFormation stack parameter (required when ApiGatewayVisibility=PRIVATE).&#xa;4. CloudFormation automatically generates the private API&#39;s resource policy from that parameter on every deploy — restricting execute-api:Invoke to that VPCE via aws:SourceVpce. No manual policy edit.&#xa;5. DNS resolution for the execute-api hostname already works today (VPC&#39;s built-in Route 53 resolver in the Network account&#39;s VPC, or the existing corporate DNS conditional forwarder + Resolver&#xa;    Inbound Endpoint over VPN/DX) — nothing new to configure for DNS.&#xa;6. No ACM certificate, no AWS RAM resource share, and no Domain Name Access Association are required in this model — those are exclusively needed for the custom-domain (Path B) feature.&#xa;7. Users access the app at the raw URL: https://&lt;api-id&gt;.execute-api.&lt;region&gt;.amazonaws.com/api/ — this is the same URL your Okta/SAML integration already validated end-to-end.&#xa;8. This scales cleanly across DEV/UAT/PROD/DR/future projects: one parameter value per environment, entirely self-service within the Application account." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="235" y="628" width="1070" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" parent="1" source="user" target="corp-dns" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
